<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 21.16 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 21.16 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said Tuesday evening.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	21.16	    +257	    20.59     22.00</p>
<p>91-Day	22.81	    +163	    22.60     22.95</p>
<p>182-Day     23.33	    +86	     23.18     23.47</p>
<p>364-Day     24.49				23.99     24.69</p>
<p>Last week the 342-day paper was assigned at 23.53 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.86 bln pesos     3.58</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   4.34 bln pesos     5.43</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   3.31 bln pesos     4.14</p>
<p>364-Day     600 million pesos   1.55 bln pesos     2.58</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.02</p>
<p>on demand of 12.06 billion pesos compared to 2.57 the week</p>
<p>before on demand of 7.72 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   84 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   14 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  14 basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			  20 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
